    <h1>Chapter 6: Generative AI</h1>

    <div class="callout info">
      <div class="callout-title">📚 Chapter Overview</div>
      <p>Generative AI creates new content—images, text, audio, video—by learning patterns from training data. This chapter explores the core architectures: GANs, VAEs, and Diffusion Models, focusing on breakthrough systems like Stable Diffusion, DALL-E, and Midjourney.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What is Generative AI?</h2>

    <p>Generative AI models learn the underlying probability distribution of training data to generate new, similar samples:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Goal:</strong> Generate novel, high-quality samples (images, text, audio)</li>
      <li><strong>Key Property:</strong> Captures data distribution P(X)</li>
      <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Art creation, design, data augmentation, content generation</li>
      <li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Balance between quality, diversity, and controllability</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Three Major Architectures</h2>

