    <h2>3. Diffusion Models (2015-2024)</h2>

    <h3>The Current State-of-the-Art</h3>

    <p>Diffusion models have become the dominant approach for high-quality image generation, powering Stable Diffusion, DALL-E 2/3, Imagen, and Midjourney.</p>

    <h3>Core Concept</h3>

    <p>Learn to reverse a gradual noising process:</p>

    <pre><code>Forward Process (Fixed):
Clean Image x₀ → + noise → x₁ → + noise → ... → xₜ → Pure Noise

Reverse Process (Learned):
Pure Noise → denoise → xₜ₋₁ → denoise → ... → x₁ → x₀ Clean Image

Training:
1. Take clean image x₀
2. Sample timestep t
3. Add noise: xₜ = √(ᾱₜ)x₀ + √(1-ᾱₜ)ε, where ε ~ N(0,I)
4. Train neural network to predict the noise ε
5. Loss = ||ε - ε_θ(xₜ, t)||²

Generation:
1. Start with pure noise xₜ
2. Iteratively denoise using learned model
3. After T steps, obtain clean image x₀</code></pre>

    <h3>Key Advantages</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Quality:</strong> State-of-the-art image fidelity</li>
      <li><strong>Stability:</strong> No adversarial training, stable convergence</li>
      <li><strong>Mode Coverage:</strong> Captures full data distribution</li>
      <li><strong>Controllability:</strong> Easy to add conditioning (text, class labels)</li>
      <li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Scales to high-resolution images</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Latent Diffusion Models (Stable Diffusion)</h3>

    <p>Breakthrough: Perform diffusion in compressed latent space (Rombach et al., 2022)</p>

    <pre><code>┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│    Latent Diffusion Model Architecture           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                  │
│  Text Prompt ──→ [CLIP Text Encoder]            │
│                         ↓                        │
│                  Text Embeddings                 │
│                         ↓                        │
│  Random Noise ──→ [U-Net Denoiser] ←─ Timestep │
│     (latent)          ↓ (cross-attention)        │
│                   Denoised Latent                │
│                         ↓                        │
│                  [VAE Decoder]                   │
│                         ↓                        │
│                   Final Image                    │
│                                                  │
│  Key Innovation: Diffusion in 64x smaller space  │
│  • 512x512 image → 64x64 latent                 │
│  • 8x faster than pixel-space diffusion         │
│  • Enables consumer GPU generation              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>

