    <h2>Text-to-Image Generation Pipeline</h2>

    <h3>How Text Prompts Control Generation</h3>

    <pre><code>1. Text Encoding:
   "A cat wearing a hat" → CLIP Text Encoder → Text Embeddings

2. Cross-Attention Conditioning:
   U-Net denoiser uses cross-attention to align image features with text

   For each U-Net layer:
   Q (queries) = image features
   K, V (keys, values) = text embeddings
   Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax(QK^T / √d) V

3. Iterative Denoising:
   Start with noise, gradually denoise guided by text embeddings

4. CFG (Classifier-Free Guidance):
   noise_pred = noise_unconditional + scale * (noise_conditional - noise_unconditional)

   • Higher scale = stronger text adherence
   • Lower scale = more creativity
   • Typical: scale = 7-15</code></pre>

    <h3>Advanced Techniques</h3>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>ControlNet (2023):</strong> Spatial control via edge maps, poses, depth
        <ul>
          <li>Add conditioning inputs (Canny edges, OpenPose skeletons)</li>
          <li>Fine-grained control over composition</li>
          <li>Compatible with any Stable Diffusion model</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation):</strong> Lightweight fine-tuning
        <ul>
          <li>Train only small adapter layers (~5-100MB)</li>
          <li>Learn specific styles, characters, concepts</li>
          <li>Mix multiple LoRAs for combined effects</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Inpainting/Outpainting:</strong> Edit specific regions
        <ul>
          <li>Masked region generation</li>
          <li>Seamless blending with original</li>
          <li>Extend images beyond borders</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Image-to-Image:</strong> Transform existing images
        <ul>
          <li>Start from encoded image + noise</li>
          <li>Control transformation strength (0-1)</li>
          <li>Style transfer, variations, modifications</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prompt Engineering for Image Generation</h2>

    <h3>Effective Prompt Structure</h3>

    <pre><code>Good Prompt Template:
[Subject] [Action/Pose] [Setting/Environment] [Style] [Lighting] [Quality Modifiers]

Examples:

Basic:
"A cat"

Improved:
"A fluffy orange cat, sitting on a windowsill, looking outside,
golden hour lighting, photorealistic, 8k, detailed fur"

Advanced:
"Portrait of a cyberpunk samurai, neon-lit Tokyo street background,
rain-soaked pavement reflections, cinematic lighting, by Artgerm and
Greg Rutkowski, trending on ArtStation, highly detailed, 8k"</code></pre>

